{
  "title": "iOS: replace fatalError/precondition crash paths for recoverable conditions",
  "description": "AGENTS.md now exempts the iOS app from the fail-fast rule, but ramekin-ios still has about 23 fatalError/precondition calls written under it. \
Review each one and replace those that guard recoverable conditions with skip/log (DebugLogger) or a surfaced error. \
Biggest cluster: RecipeCacheStore.swift (9). \
A cached row with missing fields, or with ingredients/tags JSON that isn't valid UTF-8 or doesn't decode, crashes the app on every launch until the cache is wiped. \
Instead, drop the bad row, log it, and clear the sync cursor so the next sync rewrites it. \
The same applies to an invalid pending-sweep blob in UserDefaults: clear it and restart the sweep. \
Others to review: CoreDataStack.swift (store load / model load; a store that fails to load could be deleted and recreated, since it only holds caches and pending shopping-list edits, but losing pending edits needs thought), ShoppingListStore.swift, SearchNormalizationSupport.swift (bundled contract JSON; arguably a build defect, so it can stay), RecipeSearchSupport.swift (routing preconditions), RecipeSyncSweep.swift ('hasMore with no recipes' from the server; treat as a sync error instead), WallClockBudgetSupport.swift, Shared/RamekinAPI+GeneratedClient.swift. \
Programmer-error invariants that can't be reached from data (e.g. bundled resources) can stay. \
Add unit tests that feed corrupt cache rows and check that the app recovers instead of crashing.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
